PREREQUISITES: 
The vNIC must already be added to the LPAR manually before
running this test. This script does NOT provision the vNIC itself.

input parameters:
hmc_pwd ---> HMC password
hmc_username ---> HMC user name
manageSystem ---> Provide the HMC managed system name of the CEC
slot_num ---> Virtual slot number on which the vNIC interface exists.
mac_id ---> MAC address of the vNIC interface.
                Example: "02:03:03:03:03:01"
device_ip ---> IP address to be configured on the vNIC interface after
               DLPAR.
netmasks ---> Netmask value for the vNIC interface.
               Example: "255.255.255.0"
peer_ip ---> Peer IP to ping after DLPAR to verify backend traffic.
           
sriov_adapters ---> physical location code (DRC) of
                    the SRIOV backing adapter(s) assigned to the
                    hypervisor. Used to resolve adapter_id from HMC.
                    Example: "U78DA.ND0.WZS0027-P0-C11"
sriov_ports ---> port number(s) of the SRIOV backing
                 adapter(s). Example: "0" or "0 1"
num_of_dlpar ---> Number of DLPAR remove/add cycles to perform per
                  slot. Default: 1
lockdown_enable ---> Set to True to enable kernel lockdown before
                     running DLPAR in test_vnic_dlpar_lockdown.
                     Default: False
lockdown_mode ---> Kernel lockdown mode to activate when
                   lockdown_enable is True.
                   Accepted values: integrity, confidentiality
                   Default: integrity

Example Usage:
avocado run vnic_dlpar.py -m vnic_dlpar.py.data/vnic_dlpar.yaml
avocado run vnic_dlpar.py:VnicDlpar.test_vnic_dlpar -m vnic_dlpar.py.data/vnic_dlpar.yaml
avocado run vnic_dlpar.py:VnicDlpar.test_vnic_dlpar_lockdown -m vnic_dlpar.py.data/vnic_dlpar.yaml
